Although i like zombies stuff and i enjoy the homonym series, i wasn't expecting much from this title, cause this is not my favorite videogame genre...to be honest, i decided to pick it up cause it was on a huge discount, and only based of how well the others talked about it.
But i found myself surprised...the game seems (i've not finished it yet) really good.
-It features an unique story, with some resemblances with the series;
-the story flows like an interactive film, which is great;
-there are many decisions that have to be taken, and you have limited time, like in a real life situation (this is prolly the greatest aspect of the game, really well realized);
-graphics and audio wise, the title is just ok, it has a cartoonish style, but some zombies are still "scary" and some scenes are visually nice;
That's all for now, cause i'm writing this at 1/4 of chapter 2.

A very impressive game for Alpha. I think the gameplay and visuals are very well polished, and this is an excellent capital ship MOBA. Some good things:
1) excellent come back mechanics. I have come back from pretty bad beatings;
2) Visually stunning, the game looks great;
3) excellent balance between different classes and roles of ships.
The issues, in my experience are:
1) the game takes a fairly long time to load compared to almost every other game I own (not a big deal);
2) it can take a while to queue for a game. In my experience the shortest time I've waited is 2 minutes and the longest was about 12. That being said, in games I mostly play against bots so I'm not used to waiting for queues with humans;
3) there are no bots. For many people this might not be an issue, but I'm not that interested in playing against people, and it would be nice to play against relatively competent bots like in other MOBAs (e.g. Heroes of the Storm).
Overall, I think the game is in a good place already and will only get better. I would love to see bots implemented and then I would play more often.

